# Spring Boot CRUD API

A Spring Boot REST API demonstrating CRUD operations for employees using Spring Data JPA and `JpaRepository`.

## Overview

This project is part of my Spring Boot learning journey.

The project initially used a custom DAO implementation with JPA `EntityManager` to perform database operations. It was later refactored to use Spring Data JPA and `JpaRepository`, reducing the amount of boilerplate code required for database access.

The API supports full CRUD operations as well as partial updates using HTTP PATCH.

## Project Evolution

### Version 1 - Custom DAO

The project initially used a custom DAO layer with JPA `EntityManager`.

    REST Controller
          ↓
    Service Layer
          ↓
    DAO Interface
          ↓
    DAO Implementation
          ↓
    JPA EntityManager
          ↓
    MySQL Database

### Version 2 - Spring Data JPA

The custom DAO interface and implementation were replaced with a Spring Data JPA repository.

    REST Controller
          ↓
    Service Layer
          ↓
    EmployeeRepository
          ↓
    JpaRepository
          ↓
    MySQL Database

This refactoring simplified the data access layer by using the built-in CRUD operations provided by `JpaRepository`.

## Features

- Get all employees
- Get an employee by ID
- Create a new employee
- Update an employee
- Delete an employee
- Partial update using HTTP PATCH
- JSON request and response handling
- Spring Data JPA
- `JpaRepository`
- Service layer
- REST Controller
- MySQL database integration

